const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"研究问题",en:"Research question"},body:{zh:"论文将函数逼近表述为逐步优化，并在给定损失函数下发展用于回归和分类的梯度提升程序。 阅读时应将其放回原始样本、时点和制度环境中理解，不能把问题本身当作跨市场结论。",en:"The paper frames function approximation as stagewise optimization and develops gradient-boosting procedures for regression and classification under specified loss functions. Read it as a bounded question, not as a conclusion that automatically travels beyond its sample, dates, or institutional setting."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1214/aos/1013203451",label:{zh:"The Annals of Statistics · DOI record · 来源说明",en:"The Annals of Statistics · DOI record · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"研究设计",en:"Research design"},body:{zh:"它通过连续降低损失构建加性函数，弱学习器、损失函数、停止规则和验证方案共同定义模型，而不是“提升”一词本身。 比较对象、观察窗口和对照关系共同构成研究合同；改变其中任一选择，可能改变所检验的命题。",en:"It builds an additive function through sequential loss-reducing updates, with weak learner, loss, stopping rule, and validation procedure defining the model rather than the word 'boosting' alone. The comparison, observation window, and control relation are part of the research contract; changing one can change the proposition being tested."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1214/aos/1013203451",label:{zh:"The Annals of Statistics · DOI record · 来源说明",en:"The Annals of Statistics · DOI record · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"数据与时点",en:"Data and timing"},body:{zh:"需要结果变量、预测时可得的特征、训练与留出观测、损失函数、弱学习器设置、正则或停止选择，以及时间序列数据的顺序切分。 字段定义、可得时点和样本筛选必须与原研究分开记录，不能因变量同名或使用最新修订值便视为可比。",en:"Inputs require an outcome, feature definitions available at prediction time, training and held-out observations, loss function, weak-learner settings, regularization or stopping choices, and a chronological split when data are time ordered. Keep fields, availability timing, and sample filters separate from the original study: a same-named variable or later-revised database is not automatically comparable."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1214/aos/1013203451",label:{zh:"The Annals of Statistics · DOI record · 来源说明",en:"The Annals of Statistics · DOI record · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"如何理解结果",en:"How to read the result"},body:{zh:"论文提供优化与建模框架，并不说明柔性模型具有经济含义、稳定表现或金融应用中的可交易优势。 它只支持来源描述的经验或理论关系，不能把相关性、模型拟合或历史表现升级为因果、可执行性或未来保证。",en:"The article supplies an optimization and model-building framework; it does not show that a flexible model has economic meaning, stable performance, or a tradable edge in a financial application. This remains the empirical or theoretical relation described by the source; it does not turn association, fit, or historical performance into causality, an executable procedure, or a future guarantee."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1214/aos/1013203451",label:{zh:"The Annals of Statistics · DOI record · 来源说明",en:"The Annals of Statistics · DOI record · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"复核清单",en:"Replication checks"},body:{zh:"冻结目标时点和特征可得性；只用验证集调参；记录树、学习率和迭代设置；评估校准与漂移；保留所有候选设定。 开展后续分析前，应将这些选择写入版本化研究记录，并保留原始来源链接与访问日期。",en:"Freeze target timing and feature availability; use validation not test data for tuning; record tree, learning-rate, and iteration settings; evaluate calibration and drift; and retain all candidate specifications. Before extending the analysis, record these choices in a versioned note and retain the primary-source link and access date."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1214/aos/1013203451",label:{zh:"The Annals of Statistics · DOI record · 来源说明",en:"The Annals of Statistics · DOI record · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"适用边界",en:"Scope boundary"},body:{zh:"该条导读引用 The Annals of Statistics · DOI record。通用预测算法不能替代因果识别、时点数据控制或执行与风险评估。 如需数值结论、参数、表格或稳健性检验，请回到原文并单独核对版本、附录与样本定义。",en:"This guide cites The Annals of Statistics · DOI record. A generic predictive algorithm cannot substitute for causal identification, point-in-time data controls, or an execution and risk assessment. For numerical conclusions, parameters, tables, or robustness tests, return to the original and separately verify the edition, appendices, and sample definitions."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1214/aos/1013203451",label:{zh:"The Annals of Statistics · DOI record · 来源说明",en:"The Annals of Statistics · DOI record · source description"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"本文只整理“Greedy Function Approximation: A Gradient Boosting Machine”公开说明的研究对象、设计与适用边界，不构成收益预测、交易规则或全文复现。通用预测算法不能替代因果识别、时点数据控制或执行与风险评估。",en:"This guide only organizes the publicly described question and design of “Greedy Function Approximation: A Gradient Boosting Machine”. It is not a return forecast, trading rule, or full-text replication. The source's stated scope remains controlling."}};export{e as default};
